#!/bin/bash
# Grid Trust loop — self-paced; new session: /loop $(tail -1 GRID_LOOP.sh)
# Roadmap: docs/GRID_TRUST_ROADMAP.md (doctrine §0, anchors §1, constraints §2, ledger §6)

Read docs/GRID_TRUST_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task in Section 6; the task's spec text is the requirement, the regression-table rows it names are the acceptance tests. TRUTH: never invent data, thresholds, or API behavior — read the actual anchors first (gridResearch.ts, gridTrust.ts, gridTrustRunner.ts, GridView.tsx, gridRunStore.ts, gridStore.ts); trust grades are earned per doctrine (LLM-only caps at C, A needs 2-round stability, honesty never punished); verification prompts must be adversarial per Section 5 — never "confirm the following". Reuse existing plumbing: runGridCell deps seam, extractFigures/figuresChanged, reportQaGates house style (pure fn + numbered regression test); no parallel pipelines, no new npm deps (check package.json first), no Supabase client reads of financials/chunks (anon RLS — go through searchGravity). Only DeepSeek is a live LLM; verify with unit tests + mocked deps, live probes only via npm run probe (GT-7). A task is done only when: its numbered regression tests are green via npx vitest run (from apps/market-ui/), npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json is 0 errors, existing grid tests (gridResearch.sources.test.ts, gridRunStore.test.ts, EdgarLink.test.ts) stayed green, and vercel --prod from repo root ran IF UI changed. Then flip the ledger line to [x], append ONE Section 7 Progress-log line with REAL numbers (test counts, grades from actual runs — no adjectives), and commit on roadmap/world-class with message "feat(grid-trust): GT-n <what> — <verify numbers>" (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). Never git push unless asked. PERSISTENCE: never end the loop on usage/rate limit or 429/overload — stop consuming tokens immediately, ScheduleWakeup 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger + Progress log and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log = recovery state); log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations; chain hourly wakeups as many times as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining in Section 6, or a task blocked on user-only input (credentials/infra) — then say exactly what's needed, ledger-note it, skip to the next unblocked [ ] task if one exists, and only if ALL remaining are blocked ScheduleWakeup 3600s so the loop resumes when unblocked.
